  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 153 AM MDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nHigh res models show another day of isolated to scattered thunderstorms\nacross central and east Idaho. As has been the case the past \nfew days, strong gusty outflow winds are the main impact. Gusts \napproaching 50 mph are likely and even exceeding 50 mph in a few\ninstances. Heavy downpours under the core of the storms along \nwith small hail are possible as well. The ridge amplifies over \nus on Saturday bringing heat of around 100 degrees to much of \nthe area. Good chance that we may see heat products issued once \nagain. Looks like that we get enough dry air that we'll see a \nbreak from the thunderstorms.\n\nA dry cold front arrives on Sunday which brings cooler weather to \nthe area for the first half of next week. Weather looks continued \ndry during this time. Winds over the weekend look breezy but not \nstrong enough for wind advisories.",
